          "distinct": false,
          "id": "583106a76d6c474f245a03b263a1e700d5717ce8",
          "message": "feat(routing): implementation chains lead with sol (credit abundance, cross-provider review auto-flips) (#3524)\n\n* feat(routing): implementation chains lead with sol (credit abundance, cross-provider review auto-flips)\n\nMaintainer directive 2026-07-18: heavy sol usage for implementation (abundant\ncredits; capability order opus < luna < fable < sol). Reviews are cross-provider\nvs the content author and handled pipeline-side, so sol-authored implementation\nwork receives Anthropic review automatically.\n\nFlip the implementation-side model chains to sol-first (orchestration/routing.toml only):\n  - role impl:  [\"fable\", \"sol\", \"opus\"] -> [\"sol\", \"fable\", \"opus\"]\n  - role ci:    [\"fable\", \"sol\"]         -> [\"sol\", \"fable\"]\n  - role perf:  [\"fable\", \"opus\"]        -> [\"sol\", \"fable\", \"opus\"]\n  - [defaults]: [\"fable\", \"sol\", \"opus\"] -> [\"sol\", \"fable\", \"opus\"]\n\nUntouched: the zk/mpc/crypto/auth/e2ee security-label override (opus + human\nescalate), role site (already sol-first), role research/docs/review/soundness,\nand the [models] catalog.\n\nrouting-validate.py passes (all chain models in catalog; no empty chains). The\nroute-resolve.py / dispatch-plan.py --self-test fixtures hard-code the prior\nfable-first ordering (not CI-wired; tracked in #3423) and are left for a\ncompanion refresh per the routing.toml-only scope.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test+docs: refresh routing fixtures to sol-first + fix header contradiction (sol r1)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-19T02:22:09Z",
          "tree_id": "350f796156f090b5b4ee0d62314cd966778fc25f",
